### Commit 6 · B377-3 · a deep link opened while signed out lands on the list after sign-in (Minor; AUTH SURFACE)
- **Current (MEASURED):** `proxy.ts:93` `needsSignIn(request) ? NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/", request.url), 307)` carries no path; `needsSignIn` `:64-70` leaves `/`, `/follow-up` and `/follow-up/*` open. `beginSignIn` `entra.ts:190-206` seals `Tx = { v, s, n, t }` (`:46`) into a cookie; `completeSignIn` ends `:237` with `redirect(303, "/", [clearTx, ...cookies])`; the sign-in link is a plain `<a href="/api/auth/signin">` (`SignInScreen.tsx:142`); signed in, `/` sends the person to `START[role]` client side (`SignInScreen.tsx:109-111`). B377: signed-out `/customers/{id}/report` → 307 → `/`; after sign-in the landing is `/workspace` (`evidence/shots/J7_02_deep-link-signed-out.png`, `WALK_ERROR.png`).
- **Design (you write the lines; this is the part that earns the C3 row):** (a) NEW `web/src/server/auth/returnPath.ts` exports `safeReturnPath(raw: unknown): string | null`, **path only** (no query, no fragment, no scheme, no host), accepting a value only if ALL hold: a string of at most 300 characters; every character in `[A-Za-z0-9._~/-]` (so no `%`, `\`, `:`, `?`, `#`, control character or non-ASCII); starts with exactly one `/`; no `//`; no `.` or `..` path segment; first segment in an allow-list of the signed-in routes (derive it from the `page.tsx` files under `web/src/app/(app)`: customers, workspace, home, assessments, playbook, action-plan, coach, documents, engagements, help, metrics, revenue, services, settings, admin, and any other you find; a test reads that folder and fails if a first segment is missing from the list, control: a planted missing segment is flagged); never `/`, `/api/*`, `/_next/*`, `/follow-up*`. (b) `proxy.ts:93`: when `needsSignIn` is true and `safeReturnPath(request.nextUrl.pathname)` is not null, redirect to `/` with `?next=<that path>` (URLSearchParams); otherwise exactly as today. (c) `page.tsx` reads `searchParams.next`, validates it with `safeReturnPath` again and passes the validated value (or nothing) to `SignInScreen`, which adds `?next=<encoded>` to the existing link; no other change, no word. (d) `beginSignIn` reads `next` from its own request URL, validates it again, and seals the result into the Tx as a new optional field (e.g. `r`); it is NEVER put on the Entra authorize URL or in `state`. (e) `completeSignIn` redirects to `tx.r` re-validated at the moment of use, else `/` (an old in-flight Tx without the field redirects to `/`: say you tested it). A refused value logs a reason with no value (the file's rule at `entra.ts:212`). The off-site target is refused at (a), (c), (d) and (e), by four checks that each have a row.
- **Rows, RED at base:** `returnPath.test.ts`: accepted: `/customers/CUST-01a0ff54-bf32-7b14-9aa0-aa17b1a3c4ee/report`, `/playbook/snapshot-assessment`, `/assessments/readiness/<uuid>`, `/home`; refused (each its own labelled row): `//evil.test`, `/\evil.test`, `\\evil.test`, `https://evil.test`, `javascript:alert(1)`, `data:text/html,x`, `/%2F%2Fevil.test`, `/%5Cevil`, `/customers/%0d%0aSet-Cookie:a=b`, a raw CR/LF/TAB/NUL inside, `/customers/../../x`, `/customers//x`, `/./x`, `/` , `/api/auth/signout`, `/_next/static/x`, `/follow-up/abc`, an empty string, `undefined`, a number, an array, a 10 KB string, a Unicode division slash `/∕evil.test`, a full-width `／evil`. `proxy.auth.test.ts`: hosted, signed out, `/customers/<id>/report` → 307 whose `location` is `/?next=%2Fcustomers%2F<id>%2Freport`; `/no-such-page` and `/` keep today's plain `/`; the existing `sentToSignIn` rows stay green unedited (they test the pathname only). `auth.test.ts` (against the local stand-in, with the `signIn()` helper's shape): `beginSignIn` with `?next=/customers/X/report` then `completeSignIn` → `location` is `/customers/X/report`; with `?next=//evil.test` and `?next=https://evil.test` → `/`; the authorize URL and `state` contain neither the path nor the word `next`; a forged Tx cookie (wrong key) is refused as today; an old Tx without `r` → `/`. `page.test.tsx`/`SignInScreen.test.tsx`: the link carries `?next=` only for a valid value.
- **Mutants:** m3-a accept `//` (the `//evil.test` row goes red); m3-b drop the character allow-list (the `\`, `%2F`, CR LF rows go red); m3-c drop the first-segment allow-list (`/api/auth/signout` goes red); m3-d `completeSignIn` uses the unvalidated sealed value (a forged-in-test Tx with `r: "https://evil.test"`, sealed with the test key, goes red); m3-e `beginSignIn` skips validation (red at the end-to-end row); m3-f put the path on the authorize URL (red); m3-g the proxy forwards the query string (a `?x=1` row goes red). Report each mutant's red rows BY NAME and any existing row it turns red.
- Commit: `B377-3: a signed-out deep link returns the person to the page after sign-in (same-site path only, allow-listed, sealed in the sign-in transaction)`.

### Commit 7 · B377-2 · sign-out stops on Microsoft "Pick an account" (Minor; AUTH SURFACE; do it LAST)
- **Current (MEASURED):** `entra.ts:314-335` `signOut`: after the local session is revoked (`:318-320`) it builds the end-session URL from metadata (`:323-328`) with `post_logout_redirect_uri` = `${origin(req, cfg)}/` only and no hint; `lib/entra-session.ts:23-36` navigates the browser there. The session holds `{ v: 2, sid, name, at, atExp, rt, start }` (`:48`, set `:231-234`); the ID token's claims (`id`, `:228`) are read for `tid` and `name` / `preferred_username` and then dropped. The existing test `auth.test.ts:299-312` asserts the URL and `post_logout_redirect_uri` = `${WEB}/`. B377: the sign-out lands on `login.microsoftonline.com/.../oauth2/v2.0/logout` "Pick an account"; the next "Sign in" re-enters as Admin with no credential (`evidence/shots/WALK_ERROR.png`, `evidence/log_run-walk2.log` "J7 SIGN-OUT").
- **Rules (hard, because this is a sign-out for a shared laptop):** the hint is **never a token** (no part of `at`, `rt` or the ID token, and no `id_token_hint`); it is **never logged**; it goes only on the end-session URL that `signOut` already returns in a `no-store` JSON body to a same-origin POST that passed `guard(req)`; it is stored only in the existing sealed, HttpOnly session cookie, capped at 200 characters, and `fitsSession` (the cookie budget) still decides whether the session is issued. `post_logout_redirect_uri` stays exactly `${origin}/` (return to the site's `/`).
- **Which claim is the hint is the design decision (record it with its source):** the drafter's recollection is that Microsoft documents `logout_hint` as the value of the ID token's optional **`login_hint`** claim and advises against using a UPN or e-mail there (UNMEASURED: not read; if you can read Microsoft's own page without touching the hosted site, quote it, else mark it UNMEASURED). Implement: in `completeSignIn`, read `login_hint` from the validated ID-token claims (a string, 1-200 characters, else none) and keep it in the session as a new optional field (e.g. `h`; the session stays `v: 2`, so existing sessions stay valid: test it); in `signOut`, when the unsealed session has the field, `u.searchParams.set("logout_hint", h)`; with no field behave exactly as today. **Do NOT fall back to `preferred_username` or `name`** unless STATUS shows Microsoft's documentation allows it (default: no fallback). Consequence to state in STATUS and FOR TUESDAY: the local stand-in issues no `login_hint` claim and `web/e2e` is not yours, so a real end-to-end proof is impossible here, and **if the hosted tenant's web app registration does not emit the `login_hint` optional claim the fix is inert on the hosted site until it does** (a tenant setting; also UNMEASURED whether `post_logout_redirect_uri` is registered on that app registration). Neither is yours to change.
- **Rows, RED at base:** extract the claim read into a small exported pure function (e.g. `hintFrom(claims)`) and test it: a 200-character string accepted; 201, empty, a number, an object, absent → none; a value containing a control character → none. `auth.test.ts`: a session sealed in the test with `h: "opaque-hint-0123"` (the shape `proxy.auth.test.ts:21` uses) → `signOut`'s `redirect` URL has `logout_hint=opaque-hint-0123` and `post_logout_redirect_uri` = `${WEB}/`; a session without the field → no `logout_hint` key and the existing assertions unchanged; **no token in the URL:** the URL contains no substring of 12+ characters of the session's `at` or `rt`, or of the stand-in's ID token (control: a mutant that appends `at` is flagged by this same row); the session cookie sealed with the field still unseals, and one with a 5 KB hint is refused by the cap / `fitsSession` as today; the sign-out response is `no-store`; a cross-site POST is still 403 (the existing row); no `console.warn`/`log` line in the file mentions the hint (scan). **Mutants:** m2-a hint dropped; m2-b hint taken from `name`; m2-c hint = the access token (the no-token row goes red); m2-d hint put in `post_logout_redirect_uri`; m2-e hint set when absent as the string `undefined`; m2-f cap removed (the 201-character row goes red); m2-g `post_logout_redirect_uri` changed from `/`.
- Commit: `B377-2: sign-out passes the signed-in account's login_hint claim to Entra's end-session endpoint so it signs that account out without the account picker (no token, never logged)`.

